From: meenmachine1 <78238681+meenmachine1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:41:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Decompiler: fail cleanly instead of dividing by zero in
 SplitDatatype::buildPointers

RuleSplitStore and RuleSplitLoad (SplitDatatype::splitStore/splitLoad) back
up from the LOAD/STORE pointer through PTRSUB/INT_ADD/PTRADD to a root
pointer (RootPointer::backUpPointer), accepting any pointer to a struct or
array. If that struct has size 0 (an incomplete structure: a forward
declaration, or a <type> decoded with size="0", which TypeStruct still
accepts as "the old way to indicate an incomplete structure"),
buildPointers takes the "offset outside the data-type" branch and computes
curOff % tmpType->getSize(), a division by zero: SIGFPE. An array whose
elements have size 0 divides by zero the same way a few lines below.

Throw a LowlevelError before either division, so the function fails with
an error and the process survives. Only functions that crashed before are
affected. (Refusing to back up to a pointer to a zero-size type in
backUpPointer would let the split proceed from the last sized pointer;
that is a behavior change left to upstream.)

Seen when a client hands the decompiler a pointer to an opaque library
struct (struct __jmp_buf_tag *) as an incomplete, size-0 TypeStruct.
Repro: decomp_dbg, restore the attached XML (x86-64: add rdi,0x18;
mov qword [rdi],0; ret, with p typed as pointer to a size-0 struct and
RDI after the add as uint4 *), load function storeopaque, decompile.

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/subflow.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/subflow.cc
index b191cdb..ef0e011 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/subflow.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/subflow.cc
@@ -2626,6 +2626,8 @@ void SplitDatatype::buildPointers(Varnode *rootVn,TypePointer *ptrType,int4 base
       int8 newOff;
       PcodeOp *newOp;
       Datatype *newType;
+      if (tmpType->getSize() == 0)
+	throw LowlevelError("Cannot split access through pointer to zero-size data-type: " + tmpType->getName());
       if (curOff < 0 || curOff >= tmpType->getSize()) {	// An offset not within the data-type indicates an array
 	newType = tmpType;			// The new data-type will be the same as current data-type
 	newOff = curOff % tmpType->getSize();	// But new offset will be old offset modulo data-type size
@@ -2642,6 +2644,8 @@ void SplitDatatype::buildPointers(Varnode *rootVn,TypePointer *ptrType,int4 base
       if (tmpType == newType || tmpType->getMetatype() == TYPE_ARRAY) {
 	int8 finalOffset = curOff - newOff;
 	int4 sz = newType->getSize();		// Element size in bytes
+	if (sz == 0)
+	  throw LowlevelError("Cannot split access through array of zero-size elements: " + newType->getName());
 	finalOffset = finalOffset / sz;		// Number of elements
 	sz = AddrSpace::byteToAddressInt(sz, ptrType->getWordSize());
 	newOp = data.newOp(3,followOp->getAddr());
